{"name":"Egret White","hex":"#dfd9cf","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"egret","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various wading birds of the genera Egretta or Ardea that includes herons, many of which are white or buff, and several of which develop fine plumes during the breeding season.","A plume or tuft of feathers worn as a part of a headdress, or anything imitating such an ornament."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/egret"},{"term":"white","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Bright and colourless; reflecting equal quantities of all frequencies of visible light.","Of or relating to Europeans or those of European descent, regardless if their skin has cool or warm undertones."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of snow or milk; the color of light containing equal amounts of all visible wavelengths.","A person of European descent with light-colored skin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/white"}],"entries":[{"title":"Egret","blocks":[{"text":"An egret is a type of heron; they are generally long-legged wading birds that have white or buff plumage and develop fine plumes during the breeding season. Egrets are not a biologically distinct group from herons and have the same build."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Ardea_modesta.jpg/330px-Ardea_modesta.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Egret"},{"title":"White","blocks":[{"text":"White is the lightest color and is achromatic. It is the color of objects such as snow, chalk, and milk, and is the opposite of black. White objects fully reflect and scatter all the visible wavelengths of light. White on television and computer screens is created by a mixture of red, blue, and green light. The color white can be given with white pigments, especially titanium dioxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg/330px-Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Flying_great_egret_1.jpg/500px-Flying_great_egret_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Flying_great_egret_1.jpg/1280px-Flying_great_egret_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Flying_great_egret_1.jpg/500px-Flying_great_egret_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Great egret in flight","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFlying_great_egret_1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Egrets_in_AP_W_IMG_4220.jpg/500px-Egrets_in_AP_W_IMG_4220.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Egrets_in_AP_W_IMG_4220.jpg/500px-Egrets_in_AP_W_IMG_4220.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Egrets at dusk in Kolleru Lake, Andhra Pradesh, India","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEgrets_in_AP_W_IMG_4220.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/IMG_3819-01_El_Qanater_waterfalls.jpg/500px-IMG_3819-01_El_Qanater_waterfalls.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/IMG_3819-01_El_Qanater_waterfalls.jpg/1280px-IMG_3819-01_El_Qanater_waterfalls.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/IMG_3819-01_El_Qanater_waterfalls.jpg/500px-IMG_3819-01_El_Qanater_waterfalls.jpg